Subject: [PATCH] build: port sys_wait.in.h to AmigaOS clib2 (no native sys/wait.h)

clib2 provides no sys/wait.h at all (only clib4 and newlib do), so
gnulib's generated wrapper's #include_next fails:

lib/sys/wait.h:28:16: fatal error: sys/wait.h: No such file or directory

Treat it the same as native Windows, which also lacks one: skip the
include_next and rely on this file's own WIFEXITED/WEXITSTATUS/etc.
fallback definitions (already guarded with #ifndef).

--- a/lib/sys_wait.in.h
+++ b/lib/sys_wait.in.h
@@ -22,8 +22,11 @@
 #endif
 @PRAGMA_COLUMNS@
 
-/* The include_next requires a split double-inclusion guard.  */
-#if !((defined _WIN32 || defined __WIN32__) && ! defined __CYGWIN__)
+/* The include_next requires a split double-inclusion guard.
+   AmigaOS (clib2) has no native <sys/wait.h> at all, same situation
+   as native Windows. */
+#if !((defined _WIN32 || defined __WIN32__) && ! defined __CYGWIN__) \
+    && !defined __CLIB2__
 # @INCLUDE_NEXT@ @NEXT_SYS_WAIT_H@
 #endif
 
-- 
